===Etymology 2===
{{ety|en|id=display|:inh|enm:schewe<ety:from<enm:schewen>>}}
From {{inh|en|enm|schewe}}, from [[#Etymology 1|the verb]] ({{m|enm|schewen}}).<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=sheu(e|pos=n|id=MED39914}}</ref><ref name="OED n.1">{{R:OED Online|pos=''n.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=1417705429}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[play]], [[dance]]{{,}} or other [[entertainment]].
#: {{ux|en|There were a thousand people at the '''show'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=4|passage=Then he commenced to talk, really talk. and inside of two flaps of a herring's fin he had me mesmerized, like Eben Holt's boy at the town hall '''show'''. He talked about the ills of humanity, and the glories of health and Nature and service and land knows what all.}}
# {{senseid|en|exhibition}} {{lb|en|countable}} An [[exhibition]] of [[item]]s.
#: {{ux|en|art '''show''';&emsp; dog '''show'''}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:Architectural Digest|date=May 2026|volume=83|issue=4|title=Farm Fresh|author=Julie Belcove|page=93
|text=Represented by Olney Gleason gallery, she was the subject of a 2025 solo '''show''' at the MSU Broad Art Museum in Michigan and recently unveiled a permanent installation at the Princeton University Art Museum.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[broadcast]] [[program]], especially a [[light entertainment]] program.
#: {{ux|en|radio '''show''';&emsp; television '''show'''}}
#: {{ux|en|They performed in the '''show'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I spotted my neighbour on the morning TV '''show'''.}}
#* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20171030003034/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-8-are-you-busy/3253185.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
#*: Every day I do my morning '''show'''.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[movie]].
#: {{ux|en|Let's catch a '''show'''.}}
# {{lb|en|AU|NZ|countable}} An [[agricultural]] [[exhibition]].
#: {{ux|en|I'm taking the kids to the '''show''' on Tuesday.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=6 Oct 1924|journal=The Examiner|location=Launceston|page=2|column=6|text=E. C. McEnulty, who won the chop at the '''show''' on Thursday, cut through a foot lying block in 34 seconds}}
# A project or presentation.
#: {{ux|en|Let's get on with the '''show'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Let's get this '''show''' on the road.}}
#: {{ux|en|They went on an international road '''show''' to sell the shares to investors.}}
#: {{ux|en|It was Apple's usual [[dog and pony show|dog and pony '''show''']].}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[demonstration]].
#: {{ux|en|'''show''' of force}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Mere display or [[pomp]] with no substance.  (Usually seen in the phrases "all show" and "for show".)
#* {{RQ:Young Love of Fame|passage=I envy none their pageantry and '''show'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The dog sounds ferocious but it's all '''show'''.}}
# Outward appearance; [[wileful]] or [[deceptive]] appearance.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|III|2|text=So may the outward '''shows''' be least themselves:<br>The world is still deceived with ornament.}}
# {{lb|en|baseball|with "the"}} The [[major league]]s.
#: {{ux|en|He played AA ball for years, but never made it to the '''show'''.}}
# {{lb|en|mining|obsolete}} A pale blue [[flame]] at the top of a [[candle]] flame, indicating the presence of [[firedamp]].<ref>{{R:Raymond Glossary}}</ref>
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[pretence|Pretence]].
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[sign|Sign]], [[token]], or [[indication]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[semblance|Semblance]]; [[likeness]]; [[appearance]].
#* {{RQ:KJV|Luke|20|46|47|text=Beware of the scribes,{{...}}which devour widows' houses, and for a '''shew''' make long prayers.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=9|passage=He through the midst unmarked, <br> In '''show''' plebeian angel militant <br> Of lowest order, passed.|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[plausibility|Plausibility]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} A [[discharge]], from the [[vagina]], of [[mucus]] streaked with [[blood]], occurring a short time before [[labor]].
# {{lb|en|military|slang}} A [[battle]]; local conflict. {{defdate|from 1892|refn=OED n.1|ref2={{R:Etymonline}}|ref2n=Etymonline}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Denis Garstin|title=The Shilling Soldiers|year=1918|url=https://archive.org/stream/shillingsoldiers00gars|location=London|publisher=Hodder and Stoughton|page=116|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/shillingsoldiers00gars/page/116/mode/1up|text=A subaltern, wearing a glengarry, came out of a house, playing with the nose of a shell. He walked a little way with me.<br/>“Going into the '''show'''?”}}
# A [[circular]] [[impression]] on [[sand]], indicating the presence of a [[clam]] by its [[siphon]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Karen Gaudette Brewer|title=Seafood Lover's Pacific Northwest|page=128
|passage=Iron Springs offers a guided clam dig for first timers or those who are rusty at spotting the clam's '''show''' at low tide. It includes a license and all the equipment you'll need to catch your limit on Copalis Beach {{...}}}}

